  <description>Jaragua National Park (Spanish: Parque Nacional Jaragua) is a Dominican national park located in Pedernales Province, in the extreme southwest of the Dominican Republic. Jaragua has a total area of 1,374 km2 (905 km2 of which are offshore marine habitats), the largest such protected area in the Caribbean.</description>
